[center][size=6][b][color=#ef6a5a]A G E N T   A R M O R Y[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Throw it. It does the aiming.[/i][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Agent-Armory/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/SeekerHero.jpg[/img][/center]

Every explosive in this game asks you to be in the right place at the right time. Aim the throw, judge the fuse, hope they are still standing there in three seconds.

[b]Agent Armory[/b] adds gadgets that do that part themselves. The first one is the [b]Cluster Seeker[/b]: a throwable pod that follows you and releases autonomous drones when something hostile gets close. More modules are planned.

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]This is a beta[/color][/b][/size]
The Cluster Seeker is feature-complete, but the balance is still a first draft. If it feels too strong, too weak, or unlocked at the wrong point, [b]say so in the Posts tab[/b].

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]The Cluster Seeker[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Throw it, and that is the whole input[/b]: no pin, no timer, no arming. The charge goes off on impact and the pod is out.
[*][b]The pod waits with you.[/b] With nothing in range it follows you instead of sitting where it landed, so an early throw is not a wasted one.
[*][b]Ten seekers[/b] burst out when enemies come close. Each one picks its own target, chases it for up to 18 seconds, and detonates on contact for 180 damage in a 4 m radius.
[*][b]They split up[/b] and divide the available targets between them rather than all ten piling onto the nearest zombie.
[*][b]The drones are ground units.[/b] Stairs and rough terrain slow them down, and a target on a roof is a target they will not reach.
[*][b]It will not eat your base.[/b] The pod itself causes negligible damage. The seekers do the actual work.
[*][b]Drone kills are your kills[/b], with normal XP and kill credit.
[*][b]Localized into 13 languages[/b]: EN, DE, ES, FR, IT, JA, KO, PL, PT-BR, RU, TR, ZH-Hans, ZH-Hant.
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Agent-Armory/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/SeekerSwarm.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]One throw, ten drones, and none of them waiting for you to aim.[/i][/center]

[center][size=4][b][color=#ef6a5a]See it work[/color][/b][/size]
[youtube]pQ4O9ZTpW90[/youtube][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]When to throw it[/color][/b][/size]
Against a tight crowd, a contact grenade thrown at the right moment still does more damage. What the Seeker buys you is [b]not having to be there[/b]. It works around a corner and keeps hunting while you back off and reload. Throw it into the room you are about to leave, not the one you are about to clear.

[b]It does almost nothing to blocks[/b], so leave the safes and the demolition work to the Timed Charge and the rockets.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Agent-Armory/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/SeekerPod.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]Landed and waiting, with the horde still a street away. It keeps up with you until something comes close enough to be worth splitting for.[/i][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]Unlocking and Crafting[/color][/b][/size]
Two ways in, and either is enough. Both work on a save you are already deep into.
[list]
[*][b]The Explosives skill unlocks it at level 35[/b], the same rank as the Timed Charge. Reading explosives magazines eventually unlocks it without requiring the schematic.
[*][b]The Cluster Seeker Schematic[/b] drops from loot and turns up at traders. Find one early and you get there ahead of the skill.
[/list]
Crafted at the [b]workbench[/b]: 3 mechanical parts, 18 gunpowder, 3 forged steel, 2 electrical parts, 2 springs. Stacks to 20.

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]Requirements and Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Tested on V 3.1.0.[/b] V 3.0.0 and V 3.0.1 loaded successfully during development but were not fully tested with this release.
[*][b]EasyAntiCheat must be disabled.[/b] Single-player and private servers.
[*][b]No other mods required.[/b]
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] every player and the server must have the mod installed.
[/list]
Install the zip with Vortex or MO2, or extract the [i]AgentArmory[/i] folder into [i]7 Days To Die/Mods/[/i], then launch with EAC off.

[b]Before removing the mod[/b], wait until no pod and no drone is alive in the world. Nothing else is touched: no blocks, no vanilla items, no world edits.

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

